<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sadiq Muhammad Khan V</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1904">1904</a>–<a href="/years/1966">1966</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Sadiq Muhammad Khan Abbasi V</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sadiq Muhammad Khan V was the last ruling nawab of Bahawalpur, succeeding as a child in 1907 and reigning until the state merged into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/west-pakistan">West Pakistan</a> in 1955. In October 1947 he acceded to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pakistan">Pakistan</a> and gave the new state generous financial help. His reign saw the irrigation works of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sutlej-river">Sutlej</a> Valley Project, and he founded Sadiq Public School in Bahawalpur in 1953.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sadiq-muhammad-khan-v.jpg" alt="Sadiq Muhammad Khan V" width="225" height="325" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Government of Bahawalpur · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sadeq_Mohammad_Khan.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
